# Review: FilePlugin

The upload path is solid and tested: `FileOperation.Create` resolves the stored MIME type with
`FileLimits.toStoredMimeType`, resolves the active storage from `Settings.backend` against the registered
`FileCapabilities.Backend` descriptors, and calls `File.fromBytes`, mapping `BlobTooLargeError` to
`FileTooLargeError`. `create.test.ts` covers inline upload, the registry default, MIME neutralizing and the
4 MB cap. Preview is well covered by stories: images go through `Media.Player`, PDFs through `PdfCanvas`
(one canvas per page, rasterized near the viewport, with render cancellation before `destroy`).

The biggest divergence is the `File` type: `type` and `size` are not on `File` but on the referenced
`Blob`. Scenario T-5 still expects an `<iframe>` for PDFs, which the code (and the spec's own F-3.2) replaced
with pdf.js canvases. `Settings` live in a `KvsStore` atom, not in the ECHO space. No test asserts
`NoBackendError` (T-9), and the wiring modules (`create-object`, `file-uploader`, surfaces, settings panel)
have no tests.

Of 36 items: 13 done, 9 untested, 10 partial, 3 diverged, 1 missing.

## Extensions

| Term      | URI                        |
| --------- | -------------------------- |
| `verdict` | `org.dxos.mdl.verdict@1.0` |

## Verdicts

```mdl
verdict File: The File object holds name, data and timestamp; type and size live on the referenced Blob.
  status: diverged
  evidence: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/sdk/types/src/types/File.ts#File]
  tests: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/sdk/types/src/types/File.test.ts]
  note: |
    `File.File` (`org.dxos.type.file@0.2.0`) declares only `name?`, `data: Ref<Blob>` and `timestamp?`. The MIME
    type and byte count are `Blob.type` and `Blob.size`; `useFileUrl` and the tests read them from the Blob.
```

```mdl
verdict BackendDescriptor: FileCapabilities.Backend carries name, description and storage, as a multi capability.
  status: done
  evidence: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-file/src/types/FileCapabilities.ts#Backend]
  tests: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-file/src/operations/create.test.ts]
```

```mdl
verdict Settings: Settings has an optional backend, but it is stored in a KvsStore atom, not in the ECHO space.
  status: diverged
  evidence: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-file/src/types/Settings.ts#Settings, github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-file/src/capabilities/settings.ts]
  tests: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-file/src/operations/create.test.ts]
  note: |
    `capabilities/settings.ts` builds the atom with `KvsStore.make` (local key-value storage). With no choice the
    upload falls through to the Blob registry's default; `DEFAULT_BACKEND_STORAGE` is `'inline'` and is only the
    settings Select's last-resort display value.
```

